  'Voyager 2 flew by the four giant planets between 1979 and 1989.', 'NASA: Voyager 2', 'https://science.nasa.gov/mission/voyager/voyager-2/'),
 ('rosetta-philae', 'how', 'Arrange these Rosetta and Philae mission milestones from earliest to latest.',
  '{"options":[{"id":"option-1","label":"Rosetta launches from French Guiana."},{"id":"option-2","label":"Rosetta flies past asteroid Lutetia."},{"id":"option-3","label":"Rosetta reaches comet 67P."},{"id":"option-4","label":"Philae touches down on comet 67P."}]}'::jsonb,
  '{"correct":["option-1","option-2","option-3","option-4"],"label":"Launch, asteroid flyby, comet arrival, touchdown"}'::jsonb,
  'Lutetia was a stop along Rosetta’s journey. The spacecraft reached the comet in August 2014 and released Philae in November.', 'ESA: Rosetta timeline', 'https://education.esa.int/rosetta_timeline/'),
 ('gemini-x', 'who', 'Which astronaut flew as pilot alongside John Young on Gemini X?',
